# Optional: fixed device names for Air780E modules.
#
# NOT REQUIRED any more.  The agent finds each module by asking it for its
# IMEI/ICCID and claiming the matching port, so it survives being moved to
# another socket and ttyACM renumbering on its own — configure `imei` in the
# [[devices]] block and leave `port` empty.  See docs/at-reference.md 3.3.
#
# Use this file only if you want a stable symlink for other tools, or prefer
# pinning modules to physical sockets.  Then set `port = "/dev/air780e-a"`.
#
# WHY BY PORT PATH AND NOT BY SERIAL: two identical modules report the same
# USB serial number (`000000000001` — confirmed on real hardware), so
# /dev/serial/by-id collides and you get one symlink for two devices.  Binding
# to the physical USB port is unambiguous — at the cost of having to keep each
# module in its own port, which is exactly what the agent's own discovery
# avoids.
#
# TO FILL THIS IN, after plugging both modules in:
#
#   1. Find the AT port on each module (three ttyACM* appear per module):
#        python -m air780e_agent.probe --scan
#
#   2. Get the USB port path and interface number of each AT port:
#        udevadm info -a /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -m3 KERNELS
#        udevadm info -a /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -m1 bInterfaceNumber
#
#   3. Replace the KERNELS values below, then:
#        sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#        ls -l /dev/air780e-*
#
# Measured on an AirM2M_780EPV_V1011: VID:PID 19d1:0001, USB port path "1-3",
# three ACM interfaces numbered 02 / 04 / 06 — 02 and 06 both answer AT, and
# +CMTI arrives on 02.

# Keep ModemManager away from these ports.  It probes every ttyACM it sees and
# will fight the agent for the port (symptom: garbled responses, random
# timeouts).  `systemctl mask ModemManager` is the blunter alternative.
# KEEP THESE TWO even if you use the agent's discovery instead of the symlinks.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="19d1", ATTR{idProduct}=="0001", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="19d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0001", ENV{ID_MM_PORT_IGNORE}="1"

# Module A — replace KERNELS with the real USB port path (e.g. "1-3").
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="19d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0001", \
  KERNELS=="REPLACE-ME-A", ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber}=="02", \
  SYMLINK+="air780e-a", GROUP="uucp", MODE="0660"

# Module B — replace KERNELS with the other USB port path.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="19d1", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0001", \
  KERNELS=="REPLACE-ME-B", ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber}=="02", \
  SYMLINK+="air780e-b", GROUP="uucp", MODE="0660"
